{"choices":[{"message":{"content":"{\n  \"chapter_proposals\": [\n    {\n      \"chapter_id\": \"Ch4\",\n      \"title\": \"外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰\",\n      \"purpose\": \"评估抗生素、PPIs、饮食等外部因素如何通过改变微生物组进而影响 ICI 疗效，特别是时间窗口和药物类别的特异性。\",\n      \"scope\": \"涵盖抗生素、质子泵抑制剂、其他合并用药（阿片类、类固醇、二甲双胍等）、饮食模式、生活方式（睡眠、节律）对 ICI 疗效的观察性关联证据及潜在机制。明确区分观察性关联与因果推断，标注肿瘤类型特异性及混杂因素限制。\",\n      \"excluded_source_handles\": [\n        \"P0331\",\n        \"P0371\",\n        \"P0277\"\n      ],\n      \"substantive_threads\": [\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"抗生素暴露的时机、剂量与肿瘤特异性效应\",\n          \"argument\": \"抗生素使用与 ICI 疗效下降的关联在多数实体瘤（NSCLC、黑色素瘤、RCC）中一致，但受时间窗口（ICI 启动前后 30-60 天风险最高）、疗程（>10 天风险增加）及肿瘤类型（HCC 可能无影响）调节。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0052\",\n            \"P0068\",\n            \"P0345\",\n            \"P0575\",\n            \"P0061\",\n            \"P0107\",\n            \"P0275\",\n            \"P0547\"\n          ],\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"综合多项 Meta 分析（P0052, P0068, P0345）量化抗生素暴露对 OS/PFS 的负面关联（HR 1.16-1.63），强调这是观察性数据，受感染严重程度等混杂因素影响。\",\n            \"利用 P0575 和 P0107 界定'关键时间窗'（ICI 启动前 2 个月至后 1 个月），对比 P0100 中'启动后 60 天内'的特异性影响，论证微生物完整性在免疫启动期的脆弱性。\",\n            \"引入 P0275（HCC 阴性结果）和 P0547（黑色素瘤阴性结果）作为反例，讨论肝硬化基线免疫抑制或特定菌群结构可能导致的'抗生素不敏感'现象，避免过度泛化。\",\n            \"引用 P0061 和 P0376 分析疗程长度（>10 天）及抗生素类别（氟喹诺酮类风险更高）的剂量 - 反应关系，提示广谱抗生素的破坏性更强。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"质子泵抑制剂（PPIs）与其他合并用药的独立及协同干扰\",\n          \"argument\": \"PPIs 通过改变胃酸环境导致肠道菌群'口腔化'及多样性降低，独立预测 ICI 疗效下降，且可能与抗生素存在协同负面效应；其他药物（阿片类、类固醇）证据不一，需警惕适应症偏倚。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0135\",\n            \"P0339\",\n            \"P0088\",\n            \"P0108\",\n            \"P0246\",\n            \"P0007\",\n            \"P0016\",\n            \"P0537\"\n          ],\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"基于 P0135 和 P0339 的 Meta 分析数据，确立 PPI 使用与 OS 缩短（HR=1.18）的统计关联，区分基线使用与同期使用的风险差异。\",\n            \"结合 P0088 和 P0108 阐述 PPI 导致菌群多样性降低及口腔细菌易位（P0289）的机制假说，同时指出 PPI 可能影响口服 TKI 吸收的药代动力学混淆因素。\",\n            \"利用 P0537 分析化疗与 PPI 的交互作用（近期化疗可能掩盖 PPI 效应），说明治疗背景对药物干扰效应的修饰。\",\n            \"引用 P0007 和 P0016 讨论类固醇和阿片类药物的影响，强调类固醇与 irAEs 的反向因果混淆（治疗 irAEs 而非导致），以及阿片类药物证据的异质性。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"饮食模式、益生菌与生活方式的可调节因素\",\n          \"argument\": \"高纤维饮食与 ICI 疗效正相关，而商业益生菌补充剂可能产生负面干扰；昼夜节律及心理状态通过微生物 - 免疫轴潜在调节疗效，但人类证据有限。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0155\",\n            \"P0401\",\n            \"P0390\",\n            \"P0156\",\n            \"P0249\",\n            \"P0454\",\n            \"P0224\",\n            \"P0147\",\n            \"P0453\"\n          ],\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"对比 P0155/P0401（高纤维/高脂饮食有益）与 P0390（商业益生菌可能有害）的证据，提出'食物基质优于补充剂'的假设，引用 P0156 系统综述支持高纤维饮食的 ORR 获益。\",\n            \"利用 P0249（黑覆盆子）和 P0454 讨论特定膳食成分重塑菌群功能输出的潜力，区分动物模型与人类观察性数据的证据等级。\",\n            \"引入 P0224 和 P0453 探讨昼夜节律（睡眠、给药时间）对免疫稳态的非微生物及微生物介导影响，作为外部干扰的补充维度。\",\n            \"引用 P0147 简述心理因素（抑郁）通过 HPA 轴及色氨酸代谢影响免疫的假说，强调这是新兴领域，证据多为理论推导。\"\n          ]\n        },\n        {\n          \"thread_title\": \"方法学局限与混杂因素的综合评估\",\n          \"argument\": \"现有证据多为回顾性观察，存在严重的适应症偏倚（感染本身预示预后差）及药物定义异质性；需区分'菌群介导效应'与'疾病严重程度标志'。\",\n          \"evidence_base\": [\n            \"P0012\",\n            \"P0489\",\n            \"P0524\",\n            \"P0508\",\n            \"P0463\",\n            \"P0576\"\n          ],\n          \"analysis_points\": [\n            \"利用 P0012（TKI 研究中抗生素亦降低疗效）论证抗生素影响可能部分源于非特异性机制（如全身炎症、药代动力学），而非单纯菌群介导。\",\n            \"引用 P0489 和 P0508 强调多药联用（Polypharmacy）及 I 期试验人群选择偏倚对结果的解释限制。\",\n            \"结合 P0524（医生认知调查）和 P0463（专家辩论）反映临床界对微生物干预潜力的认可与对证据异质性的担忧，指出'功能优于组成'的研究方向。\",\n            \"总结 P0576 和 P0402 关于抗生素定义（种类、时长）不一致的问题，呼吁未来研究标准化药物暴露记录及微生物组动态监测。\"\n          ]\n        }\n      ],\n      \"transition_logic\": \"本章确立了外部因素（特别是抗生素和 PPIs）对微生物 - 免疫轴的显著干扰作用，揭示了微生物组状态的'可塑性'及'脆弱性'。这为下一章（Ch5）讨论主动微生物干预策略（如 FMT、工程菌）提供了逻辑基础：如果非特异性干扰能削弱疗效，那么特异性干预理论上可能恢复或增强疗效，但需克服本章识别的混杂因素及时间窗口挑战。\",\n      \"supplement_requests\": [],\n      \"directed_reads\": [\n        \"P0052\",\n        \"P0068\",\n        \"P0135\",\n        \"P0339\",\n        \"P0275\",\n        \"P0537\",\n        \"P0390\",\n        \"P0012\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screened_sources\": [\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0331\",\n      \"reason\": \"研究对象为 CAR-T 疗法及血液肿瘤（DLBCL），与本综述聚焦的实体瘤 ICI 治疗背景不符，机制虽可类比但易混淆主题。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0371\",\n      \"reason\": \"聚焦于血液制品（PRBC）及其微生物组，而非肠道微生物组，来源及机制路径差异显著，不适用于本章核心论证。\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source_handle\": \"P0277\",\n      \"reason\": \"讨论流感疫苗对 ICI 疗效的影响，属于系统性免疫激活而非微生物组介导的外部干扰，与本章主题关联度低。\"\n    }\n  ]\n}","reasoning_content":"The user wants a chapter proposal for Chapter 4 of a review on \"How does the gut microbiome modulate the efficacy of immune checkpoint inhibitors in solid tumours, and what mechanisms mediate that effect?\".\nThe chapter title is \"外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰\" (External Factors Interfering with the Microbiome-Immune Axis).\nThe purpose is to evaluate how antibiotics, PPIs, diet, etc., affect ICI efficacy by altering the microbiome, focusing on timing and specificity.\nI need to generate a JSON response containing the chapter proposal, including title, purpose, scope, substantive threads, source handles, excluded sources (if any), supplement requests, directed reads, and transition logic.\nI must adhere to the constraints:\n- Use Chinese for the content.\n- Do not write an introduction or conclusion for the whole review (that's handled elsewhere).\n- Focus on substantive knowledge and analysis.\n- Do not simply list papers but organize them by themes/arguments.\n- Respect source routing and interpretation limits (e.g., observational data != causality).\n- Ensure the chapter fits into the shared Level 1 outline (Ch4 follows Ch3 on metabolites, precedes Ch5 on interventions).\n- Address key questions: Antibiotic timing, drug class specificity, tumor type sensitivity.\n- Use the provided source_routing information to select relevant sources for this chapter.\n- Do not discard routed sources unless genuinely out of scope (name them in excluded_source_handles if so).\n- Ensure the proposal reflects the evidence limits (e.g., retrospective nature, confounding).\n\nPlan for Chapter 4:\n1.  **Introduction/Scope**: Define external factors (medications, diet, lifestyle) that modulate the microbiome and potentially impact ICI. Emphasize the observational nature of most evidence.\n2.  **Antibiotics (ABX)**:\n    *   **Timing**: Pre-ICI vs. During-ICI vs. Post-ICI. Critical window (e.g., 30-60 days before/during).\n    *   **Class/Duration**: Broad-spectrum vs. Narrow. Duration thresholds (e.g., >10 days).\n    *   **Tumor Specificity**: NSCLC, Melanoma, RCC vs. HCC (negative/neutral results).\n    *   **Mechanism (Indirect)**: Dysbiosis leading to reduced immune priming (link to Ch2/Ch3).\n    *   **Confounding**: Infection severity, performance status.\n3.  **Proton Pump Inhibitors (PPIs)**:\n    *   **Association**: Reduced OS/PFS.\n    *   **Mechanism**: pH change -> oral bacteria translocation -> dysbiosis.\n    *   **Interaction**: With chemotherapy (may mask effect).\n4.  **Other Medications**:\n    *   **Opioids, Steroids, Metformin, Statins**: Mixed evidence, potential mechanisms.\n    *   **Polypharmacy**: Cumulative effect.\n5.  **Diet & Lifestyle**:\n    *   **Fiber/Plant-based**: Positive association (SCFA production).\n    *   **Probiotics**: Commercial vs. Natural (potential negative effect of commercial).\n    *   **Fasting/Ketogenic**: Preclinical evidence, limited human data.\n    *   **Circadian Rhythm**: Infusion timing, sleep.\n6.  **Synthesis/Transition**: Summarize the fragility of the microbiome-ICI axis to external perturbations. Transition to Ch5 (Interventions) by noting that if external factors can harm, intentional interventions might help (but require rigorous testing).\n\nSource Selection from Routing:\n- P0007 (ABX, PPI, Steroids retrospective)\n- P0012 (ABX in TKI - contrast)\n- P0016 (Opioids review)\n- P0033 (Longitudinal microbiome, PPI/ABX impact)\n- P0035 (mUC, ABX/PPI/Metformin)\n- P0036 (Narrative review ABX/Gut/ICI)\n- P0039 (Meta-analysis ABX/Probiotic/FMT)\n- P0041 (Drug-Microbiome interaction review)\n- P0052 (Meta-analysis NSCLC ABX)\n- P0053 (NSCLC, microbiome + chemo + ABX)\n- P0061 (ABX duration retrospective)\n- P0068 (Meta-analysis ABX survival)\n- P0081 (Meta-analysis diverse drug effects)\n- P0088 (PPI pharmacovigilance)\n- P0091 (Review microbiome chemo/ICI)\n- P0096 (Review Lung Cancer microbiome)\n- P0100 (ABX timing abstract)\n- P0103 (Review Crosstalk)\n- P0107 (ABX retrospective real-world)\n- P0108 (PPI review)\n- P0110 (Pancreatic cancer review)\n- P0115 (Lung cancer review)\n- P0123 (NSCLC microbial signatures + PPI)\n- P0129 (Systematic review modulating factors)\n- P0131 (Narrative review emerging role)\n- P0135 (Meta-analysis PPI)\n- P0147 (Depression review)\n- P0153 (PEG bowel prep)\n- P0155 (Diet NSCLC)\n- P0156 (Diet interventions review)\n- P0157 (Review overcoming resistance)\n- P0176 (Metabolism review)\n- P0182 (NSCLC Japanese cohort + ABX)\n- P0185 (PPI multiple cancer types)\n- P0194 (Review diagnostic/therapeutic)\n- P0195 (DAT metabolite + ABX)\n- P0198 (Fasting RCC)\n- P0201 (Polyphenol mouse)\n- P0205 (EGFR-mutated NSCLC)\n- P0206 (GU tumors review)\n- P0213 (CRC immunotherapy failure review)\n- P0224 (Sleep/Circadian review)\n- P0234 (Biomarkers review)\n- P0236 (Meta-analysis NSCLC ABX)\n- P0246 (PPI NSCLC 5-year survival)\n- P0249 (Black raspberry diet)\n- P0252 (Diet/Probiotics review)\n- P0254 (Obesity paradox review)\n- P0263 (UC review)\n- P0266 (Hispanic NSCLC ABX)\n- P0269 (Host factors review)\n- P0275 (HCC ABX negative)\n- P0277 (Flu vaccine)\n- P0279 (DNA Pol IIIC inhibitors)\n- P0286 (Drug-Drug interactions review)\n- P0288 (GI cancers patient characteristics)\n- P0289 (SCRUM-Japan MONSTAR-SCREEN)\n- P0300 (Spanish review)\n- P0304 (Systematic review drugs/FMT)\n- P0310 (Melanoma ABX + Colitis)\n- P0313 (NSCLC/Melanoma review)\n- P0321 (GI tumors microbiome group)\n- P0322 (NSCLC microbiome/irAE review)\n- P0328 (TNBC review)\n- P0331 (CAR-T ABX - analogy)\n- P0339 (Meta-analysis PPI)\n- P0341 (Diet/Microbes review)\n- P0343 (Integrative oncology review)\n- P0345 (Meta-analysis ABX)\n- P0346 (Energy balance review)\n- P0347 (Comedications review)\n- P0360 (Gynecologic ABX duration)\n- P0370 (HCC review)\n- P0371 (Blood transfusion review)\n- P0374 (Melanoma biomarkers)\n- P0376 (Older adults ABX)\n- P0389 (RCC review)\n- P0390 (Diet/Probiotics Melanoma)\n- P0401 (High fiber NSCLC)\n- P0402 (ABX therapy review)\n- P0417 (Systematic review microbiome/ICI)\n- P0418 (RCC ABX/TKI)\n- P0427 (Black raspberry mouse)\n- P0438 (GI cancer resistance review)\n- P0443 (NSCLC microbial signatures)\n- P0452 (Sucralose review)\n- P0453 (ICI infusion timing)\n- P0454 (Diet/Microbiome review)\n- P0459 (Circadian-Microbiome review)\n- P0463 (Debate report)\n- P0469 (Gut microbiota immunomodulation review)\n- P0481 (Bile acid mouse)\n- P0489 (Pan-tumor comedication)\n- P0505 (Levofloxacin + Probiotic mouse)\n- P0508 (Phase I ABX survival)\n- P0516 (GI cancers review)\n- P0517 (NSCLC ABX + PD-L1)\n- P0522 (Microbiome resistance review)\n- P0523 (Radiotherapy/Immunotherapy gut strategies)\n- P0524 (Oncologist perceptions survey)\n- P0537 (PPI + Chemo interaction)\n- P0543 (Leveraging gut microbiota review)\n- P0545 (Polish Melanoma population-specific)\n- P0547 (Systematic review ABX survival)\n- P0548 (Gut Microbiota systemic therapy review)\n- P0558 (ICI timing circadian)\n- P0560 (Gut Microbiota tumor immune escape review)\n- P0564 (Influence Microbiome ABX review)\n- P0566 (Lung cancer microbiome prediction)\n- P0571 (Molecular interplay circadian review)\n- P0575 (ABX timing survival)\n- P0576 (ABX therapy effectiveness review)\n- P0585 (JCOG2007 NSCLC chemo-immuno)\n\nI will structure the chapter to first address the most robust evidence (Antibiotics), then PPIs, then other drugs, then diet/lifestyle. I will ensure to highlight the observational nature and confounding factors as per the interpretation limits. I will exclude sources that are purely about CAR-T (P0331) or blood transfusion (P0371) unless used as a very brief analogy for immune modulation, but better to exclude to stay focused on solid tumor ICI. P0331 is CAR-T, P0371 is blood transfusion - I will exclude these as they are out of scope for \"solid tumor ICI\" focus or \"gut microbiome\" focus respectively. P0277 (Flu vaccine) is tangential but can be used for \"immune activation\" context, but maybe better to exclude to keep focus on microbiome-modulating factors. P0453 (Infusion timing) is circadian but not microbiome directly, can be used as a comparator for \"external factors\". I will keep most routed sources as they are relevant to \"External Factors\".\n\nI need to make sure I don't claim causality for observational data.\nI need to make sure I distinguish between tumor types (NSCLC, Melanoma, RCC, HCC, etc.).\nI need to make sure I mention the \"critical window\" for antibiotics.\nI need to make sure I mention the controversy/negative results (e.g., HCC, some melanoma studies).\n\nLet's draft the JSON.\nChapter ID: Ch4\nTitle: 外部因素对微生物 - 免疫轴的干扰\nPurpose: 评估抗生素、PPIs、饮食等外部因素如何通过改变微生物组进而影响 ICI 疗效，特别是时间窗口和药物类别的特异性。\nScope: 涵盖抗生素、质子泵抑制剂、其他合并用药（阿片类、类固醇、二甲双胍等）、饮食模式、生活方式（睡眠、节律）对 ICI 疗效的观察性关联证据及潜在机制。明确区分观察性关联与因果推断，标注肿瘤类型特异性及混杂因素限制。\nSubstantive Threads:\n1. 抗生素暴露的时机与剂量效应（时间窗口、疗程、广谱 vs 窄谱）。\n2. 质子泵抑制剂（PPIs）及其他合并用药的独立或协同影响。\n3. 饮食模式与营养干预（纤维、益生菌、禁食）的调节作用。\n4. 宿主生活方式因素（昼夜节律、心理状态）的潜在干扰。\n5. 肿瘤类型与治疗背景的异质性（如 HCC 的阴性结果、化疗的掩盖效应）。\nExcluded Sources: P0331 (CAR-T, out of scope), P0371 (Blood transfusion, not gut microbiome), P0277 (Flu vaccine, not microbiome focused).\nSupplement Requests: None (pool is large enough).\nDirected Reads: P0052, P0068, P0081, P0135, P0339 (Meta-analyses for ABX/PPI); P0033, P0053, P0585 (Longitudinal/Chemo-interaction); P0275, P0547 (Negative/Heterogeneous results).\n\nI will write the JSON now.","role":"assistant"},"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"logprobs":null}],"object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":35753,"completion_tokens":5287,"total_tokens":41040,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3162,"text_tokens":5287},"prompt_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":35753}},"created":1791137892,"system_fingerprint":null,"model":"qwen3.5-plus","id":"chatcmpl-1629f1c1-612b-9c24-b2e4-92c9a6601089"}